  "studentQuestionsAI": {
    "headline": "1.3 million visits this fall; course lookups dominate, career and research searches lag.",
    "summary": "Between August 22 and November 20, 2026, the COAS site drew 1,304,719 visits, nearly three-quarters of them first-time visitors. On-site searches skew heavily toward courses and exams at 16.2 percent of searches, while careers, internships, and research together account for just 2.2 percent?suggesting students who want that content may not be finding it, or may be leaving to look elsewhere.",
    "questions": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "insight": "Careers and internships made up only 1.4 percent of on-site searches, which likely reflects thin content rather than low student interest?departments supplying graduate outcome data would give us something concrete to surface."
      },
